Make codeml's branch-length convergence tolerance settable at runtime.

Forestry declares `e = 1e-8` (codeml.c:612) and passes it unchanged to minB as
e0 (codeml.c:756). minB's only convergence exit is

    if ((dl = fabs(*lnL - lnL0)) < e0 && e <= 0.02) break;

where dl is a whole round's lnL improvement. On a large tree that test cannot
fire. Measured on OG0000000 of the fish run (690 seqs, 12454 codons, 1377
branches): round improvements reach 8.5e-4 by round 11 and the per-round
epsilon then pins at minB's hardcoded 1e-6 floor, so rounds settle at ~1e-6 of
improvement each. Reaching 1e-8 from there needs 450-2300 further rounds
against a hard cap of maxr = 200, and minB's own "too slow" bail-out is gated
on ntime0 < 200 so it never fires either.

The fit therefore always runs exactly 200 rounds. Its stopping point is a round
count, not a converged optimum -- which is worth knowing before treating the
full-length fit as a gold standard it is not.

This patch lets PAML_MINB_E0 override e0 for the com.method == 1 path only.
Unset, the binary is bit-identical to stock. Nothing else reads e before the
call, so the override is complete.

Build:
    export PAML_MINB_E0=0.01   # stop once a round gains < 0.01 lnL
Suggested values, from the OG0000000 round trace:
    0.01    stops after round 8    (dl 4.896e-3 -> 1.100e-3)
    0.0015  stops after round 10   (dl 1.100e-3 -> 8.540e-4)
    unset   200 rounds

--- a/src/codeml.c
+++ b/src/codeml.c
@@
          if (iteration && np) {
-            if (com.method == 1)
-               j = minB(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, x, xb, e, com.space);
+            if (com.method == 1) {
+               /* divergence: e is the literal 1e-8 from Forestry's declaration
+                  and is unreachable on large trees; allow it to be set. */
+               const char *e0env = getenv("PAML_MINB_E0");
+               double e0 = (e0env && *e0env) ? atof(e0env) : e;
+               if (noisy && e0 != e) printf("\nminB e0 overridden: %g\n", e0);
+               j = minB(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, x, xb, e0, com.space);
+            }
             else if (com.method == 3)
                j = minB2(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, x, xb, e, com.space);
             else
                j = ming2(noisy > 2 ? frub : NULL, &lnL, com.plfun, NULL, x, xb, com.space, e, np);
